---
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<div class="res-body" style="padding: 0 48px">
  <div id="section-all" class="cat-section visible">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <div class="sec-head-icon">🧭</div>
      <div class="sec-head-text">
        <h2>All Resources</h2>
        <p>
          Every resource available to Alabama veterans, servicemembers, and their families. Use the
          filters below or search above.
        </p>
        <div class="redbar"></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="filter-row">
      <span class="filter-label">Filter by type:</span><button
        class="f-btn active"
        onclick="filterType('all', this)">All</button
      ><button class="f-btn" onclick="filterType('federal', this)">Federal</button><button
        class="f-btn"
        onclick="filterType('state', this)">State of Alabama</button
      ><button class="f-btn" onclick="filterType('local', this)">Local</button><button
        class="f-btn"
        onclick="filterType('nonprofit', this)">Nonprofits</button
      ><button class="f-btn" onclick="filterType('hotline', this)">Hotlines</button>
    </div>
    <div class="res-grid" id="all-grid"></div>
    <div class="no-results" id="no-results">
      <h3>No Resources Found</h3>
      <p>Try a different keyword or clear your search to browse everything.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div id="section-crisis" class="cat-section">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <div class="sec-head-icon">🆘</div>
      <div class="sec-head-text">
        <h2>Crisis &amp; Mental Health</h2>
        <p>
          If you or a veteran you know is struggling, help is available right now. You are not alone
          and you are not a burden.
        </p>
        <div class="redbar"></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="alert-box">
      <div class="alert-icon">📞</div>
      <div class="alert-text">
        <h3>Veterans Crisis Line — 988, Press 1</h3>
        <p>
          Free, confidential support 24 hours a day, 7 days a week. You can also text 838255 or chat
          online. One call connects you to a trained VA responder who understands what you've been
          through.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="alert-btns">
        <a href="tel:988" class="abtn-r">📞 Call 988</a><a href="sms:838255" class="abtn-o"
          >💬 Text 838255</a
        >
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="sub-label">SAFER Together — Firearm Safe Storage Program</div>
    <div class="info-box">
      <strong>About SAFER Together</strong> The Storing Ammunition and Firearms to Enhance Resilience
      Together (SAFER Together) program lets veterans, first responders, and civilians voluntarily and
      temporarily store firearms at participating gun shops during a personal crisis — no questions asked,
      completely confidential. When you feel ready, you pick them up during normal business hours. Peer
      support is available throughout the process. For resources and participating locations, visit <strong
        >vetsforhope.com</strong
      >
    </div>
    <div class="vetcenter-grid" style="margin-bottom: 3px">
      <div class="safer-card vc-card">
        <div class="vc-name">Redland Rifle Company</div>
        <div class="vc-detail"><strong>City</strong> Hoover, AL (Birmingham Metro)</div>
        <div class="vc-detail">
          <strong>Notes</strong> First Birmingham-area SAFER Together partner. Voluntary, confidential
          firearm storage with peer support referral available.
        </div>
        <a href="https://vetsforhope.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="vc-link"
          >Learn More at VetsForHope.com →</a
        >
      </div>
      <div class="safer-card vc-card">
        <div class="vc-name">My Gun Shop</div>
        <div class="vc-detail"><strong>City</strong> Pelham, AL</div>
        <div class="vc-detail">
          <strong>Notes</strong> Third statewide SAFER Together location. Four dedicated safes available
          for temporary storage during crisis periods.
        </div>
        <a href="https://vetsforhope.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="vc-link"
          >Learn More at VetsForHope.com →</a
        >
      </div>
      <div class="safer-card vc-card">
        <div class="vc-name">Additional Locations Growing</div>
        <div class="vc-detail"><strong>State</strong> Alabama Statewide</div>
        <div class="vc-detail">
          <strong>Notes</strong> The SAFER Together network is expanding across Alabama. Visit vetsforhope.com
          or contact the Birmingham VA for the most current list of participating gun shops near you.
        </div>
        <div class="vc-detail" style="margin-top: 8px">
          <strong>Contact</strong> Birmingham VA: (205) 933-8101
        </div>
        <a href="https://vetsforhope.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="vc-link"
          >Find Locations at VetsForHope.com →</a
        >
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="sub-label" style="margin-top: 40px">Mental Health Resources</div>
    <div class="res-grid" id="crisis-grid"></div>
  </div>
  <div id="section-vetcenters" class="cat-section">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <div class="sec-head-icon">🏥</div>
      <div class="sec-head-text">
        <h2>VA &amp; Vet Centers</h2>
        <p>
          VA Medical Centers, Community Based Outpatient Clinics, and Vet Centers located across
          Alabama. Vet Centers are community-based counseling centers separate from the VA hospital
          system — no appointment needed for many services, and combat veterans do not need to
          enroll in VA healthcare to use them.
        </p>
        <div class="redbar"></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="sub-label">Alabama Veterans Resource Center (AVRC)</div>
    <div class="info-box">
      <strong>Brand New in 2026</strong>
      Opened February 18, 2026 — the AVRC is a public-private partnership created by Gov. Kay Ivey and
      the Alabama Legislature to serve as a one-stop statewide hub for veterans navigating benefits, employment,
      housing, healthcare, and more. The Montgomery location is the first, with satellite offices planned
      statewide. An online digital hub is also live at missionforwardal.org.
    </div>
    <div class="vetcenter-grid" style="margin-bottom: 28px">
      <div class="vc-card" style="border-top-color: var(--red); background: var(--blue-dp)">
        <div class="vc-name" style="color: var(--white); font-size: 26px">
          Alabama Veterans Resource Center
        </div>
        <div class="vc-detail" style="color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.6)">
          <strong style="color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.35)">Address</strong> 100 Dexter Avenue, Montgomery,
          AL 36104
        </div>
        <div class="vc-detail" style="color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.6)">
          <strong style="color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.35)">Services</strong> Benefits navigation, employment,
          job training, housing assistance, mental health referrals, family support, peer connection
        </div>
        <div class="vc-detail" style="color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.6)">
          <strong style="color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.35)">Online Hub</strong>
          missionforwardal.org — statewide digital access
        </div>
        <a
          href="https://missionforwardal.org"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="vc-link">Visit missionforwardal.org →</a
        >
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="sub-label">VA Vet Centers in Alabama</div>
    <div class="info-box">
      <strong>What Is a Vet Center?</strong>
      VA Vet Centers are community-based readjustment counseling centers offering individual and group
      therapy, PTSD treatment, MST counseling, substance abuse referrals, employment assistance, and bereavement
      counseling — all in a non-clinical, community setting. Combat veterans can access Vet Center services
      regardless of VA enrollment status.
    </div>
    <div class="vetcenter-grid">
      <div class="vc-card">
        <div class="vc-name">Birmingham Vet Center</div>
        <div class="vc-detail">
          <strong>Address</strong> 400 Emery Drive, Suite 200, Hoover, AL 35244
        </div>
        <div class="vc-detail"><strong>Phone</strong> Contact VA.gov for current number</div>
        <div class="vc-detail"><strong>Hours</strong> Mon–Fri, 8:00 AM – 4:30 PM</div>
        <div class="vc-sat">
          <div class="vc-sat-label">Satellite / Mobile</div>
          <div class="vc-sat-item">
            <strong>Birmingham Mobile Vet Center (MVC)</strong> — Travels to underserved areas. Call main
            center for schedule.
          </div>
        </div>
        <a
          href="https://va.gov/birmingham-vet-center"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="vc-link">VA.gov Listing →</a
        >
      </div>
      <div class="vc-card">
        <div class="vc-name">Huntsville Vet Center</div>
        <div class="vc-detail">
          <strong>Address</strong> 415 Church Street, Building H, Suite 101, Huntsville, AL 35801
        </div>
        <div class="vc-detail"><strong>Phone</strong> Contact VA.gov for current number</div>
        <div class="vc-detail"><strong>Hours</strong> Mon–Fri, 8:00 AM – 4:30 PM</div>
        <a
          href="https://va.gov/huntsville-vet-center"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="vc-link">VA.gov Listing →</a
        >
      </div>
      <div class="vc-card">
        <div class="vc-name">Montgomery Vet Center</div>
        <div class="vc-detail">
          <strong>Address</strong> 4405 Atlanta Highway, Montgomery, AL 36109
        </div>
        <div class="vc-detail"><strong>Phone</strong> Contact VA.gov for current number</div>
        <div class="vc-detail"><strong>Hours</strong> Mon–Fri, 8:00 AM – 4:30 PM</div>
        <div class="vc-sat">
          <div class="vc-sat-label">Satellite Location</div>
          <div class="vc-sat-item">
            <strong>Troy University Campus</strong> — 321 Veterans Memorial Dr, Room 122, Troy, AL 36082.
            Appointments by request from main center.
          </div>
        </div>
        <a
          href="https://va.gov/montgomery-vet-center"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="vc-link">VA.gov Listing →</a
        >
      </div>
      <div class="vc-card">
        <div class="vc-name">Mobile Vet Center</div>
        <div class="vc-detail">
          <strong>Address</strong> 3221 Springhill Avenue, Building 2, Suite C, Mobile, AL 36607
        </div>
        <div class="vc-detail"><strong>Phone</strong> Contact VA.gov for current number</div>
        <div class="vc-detail"><strong>Hours</strong> Mon–Fri, 8:00 AM – 4:30 PM</div>
        <div class="vc-sat">
          <div class="vc-sat-label">Community Access Points</div>
          <div class="vc-sat-item">
            <strong>Chatom</strong> — Washington County Public Library, 14102 St. Stephens Ave, Chatom,
            AL 36518. Last Thursday of the month.
          </div>
          <div class="vc-sat-item">
            <strong>Fairhope</strong> — Jubilee Shores United Methodist Church, 17261 AL-181, Fairhope,
            AL 36532. Mondays by appointment.
          </div>
          <div class="vc-sat-item">
            <strong>Jackson</strong> — First Assembly of God, 2410 Coffeeville Rd, Jackson, AL 36545.
            Second Thursday of the month.
          </div>
        </div>
        <a
          href="https://va.gov/mobile-vet-center"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="vc-link">VA.gov Listing →</a
        >
      </div>
      <div class="vc-card">
        <div class="vc-name">Gadsden / Anniston Area</div>
        <div class="vc-detail">
          <strong>Coverage</strong> Served by Birmingham Vet Center outreach and the Birmingham Mobile
          Vet Center. VA CBOCs in Rainbow City (Gadsden) and Oxford also serve this region.
        </div>
        <div class="vc-detail">
          <strong>CBOC</strong> Rainbow City VA Clinic — Gadsden/Rainbow City area
        </div>
        <div class="vc-detail"><strong>CBOC</strong> Oxford VA Clinic — Anniston/Oxford area</div>
        <a
          href="https://va.gov/birmingham-health-care/locations"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="vc-link">Birmingham VA Locations →</a
        >
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="sub-label" style="margin-top: 40px">VA Medical Centers &amp; Major Clinics</div>
    <div class="res-grid" id="vetcenters-grid"></div>
  </div>
  <div id="section-housing" class="cat-section">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <div class="sec-head-icon">🏠</div>
      <div class="sec-head-text">
        <h2>Housing Resources</h2>
        <p>
          Emergency shelter, transitional housing, permanent housing, and homebuying assistance for
          Alabama veterans at every stage of need.
        </p>
        <div class="redbar"></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="info-box">
      <strong>HUD-VASH — Start Here If You Are Homeless</strong>
      The HUD-VA Supportive Housing program combines VA healthcare with HUD housing vouchers for veterans
      experiencing homelessness. Contact any Alabama VA Medical Center directly and ask specifically about
      HUD-VASH to get started. You do not need a VA disability rating to qualify.
    </div>
    <div class="res-grid" id="housing-grid"></div>
  </div>
  <div id="section-benefits" class="cat-section">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <div class="sec-head-icon">📋</div>
      <div class="sec-head-text">
        <h2>Benefits &amp; Claims</h2>
        <p>
          Free claims assistance, disability ratings, appeals, PACT Act toxic exposure benefits, and
          state-specific Alabama veteran benefits.
        </p>
        <div class="redbar"></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="info-box">
      <strong>Never Pay to File a VA Claim</strong>
      Accredited VSO representatives, ADVA county service officers, American Legion, DAV, and VFW service
      officers all help veterans file and appeal VA claims at no cost. If anyone asks for money upfront
      to file a claim, walk away — it may be a scam.
    </div>
    <div class="res-grid" id="benefits-grid"></div>
  </div>
  <div id="section-education" class="cat-section">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <div class="sec-head-icon">🎓</div>
      <div class="sec-head-text">
        <h2>Education &amp; Training</h2>
        <p>
          GI Bill, vocational rehab, Alabama tuition waivers for dependents, scholarships, and
          training programs for veterans pursuing college or a new career.
        </p>
        <div class="redbar"></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="res-grid" id="education-grid"></div>
  </div>
  <div id="section-employment" class="cat-section">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <div class="sec-head-icon">💼</div>
      <div class="sec-head-text">
        <h2>Employment &amp; Jobs</h2>
        <p>
          Resume help, veteran hiring preference, apprenticeships, entrepreneurship programs, and
          the Alabama Veterans Resource Center's job placement services.
        </p>
        <div class="redbar"></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="res-grid" id="employment-grid"></div>
  </div>
  <div id="section-financial" class="cat-section">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <div class="sec-head-icon">💰</div>
      <div class="sec-head-text">
        <h2>Financial Assistance</h2>
        <p>
          Emergency grants, Alabama property tax exemptions for disabled veterans, utility help, and
          other financial relief programs.
        </p>
        <div class="redbar"></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="res-grid" id="financial-grid"></div>
  </div>
  <div id="section-legal" class="cat-section">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <div class="sec-head-icon">⚖️</div>
      <div class="sec-head-text">
        <h2>Legal Help</h2>
        <p>
          Free legal aid, discharge upgrades, housing disputes, family law, and civil matters for
          veterans and their families in Alabama.
        </p>
        <div class="redbar"></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="res-grid" id="legal-grid"></div>
  </div>
  <div id="section-family" class="cat-section">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <div class="sec-head-icon">👨‍👩‍👧</div>
      <div class="sec-head-text">
        <h2>Family &amp; Caregivers</h2>
        <p>
          Support for military families, surviving spouses, Gold Star families, and caregivers who
          support veterans at home.
        </p>
        <div class="redbar"></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="res-grid" id="family-grid"></div>
  </div>
  <div id="section-transition" class="cat-section">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <div class="sec-head-icon">🎖️</div>
      <div class="sec-head-text">
        <h2>Transition Support</h2>
        <p>
          Resources built for servicemembers separating from active duty and veterans within their
          first few years of civilian life.
        </p>
        <div class="redbar"></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="res-grid" id="transition-grid"></div>
    <div id="section-ministry" class="cat-section">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <div class="sec-head-icon">✝️</div>
        <div class="sec-head-text">
          <h2>Ministry &amp; Faith-Based</h2>
          <p>
            Faith-centered programs and ministries serving veterans, first responders, and their
            families — retreats, peer support, and spiritual care.
          </p>
          <div class="redbar"></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="res-grid" id="ministry-grid"></div>
    </div>
    <div id="section-women" class="cat-section">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <div class="sec-head-icon">👩‍✈️</div>
        <div class="sec-head-text">
          <h2>Women Veterans</h2>
          <p>
            Resources built for the unique needs of women who served — health care, peer support,
            advocacy, and help navigating VA benefits.
          </p>
          <div class="redbar"></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="res-grid" id="women-grid"></div>
    </div>
    <div id="section-adaptive" class="cat-section">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <div class="sec-head-icon">🏅</div>
        <div class="sec-head-text">
          <h2>Adaptive Sports &amp; Recreation</h2>
          <p>
            Stay active after service. Adaptive sports, fitness, and outdoor recreation for veterans
            of every ability, including Alabama’s own Lakeshore Foundation.
          </p>
          <div class="redbar"></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="res-grid" id="adaptive-grid"></div>
    </div>
    <div id="section-recovery" class="cat-section">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <div class="sec-head-icon">🫂</div>
        <div class="sec-head-text">
          <h2>Substance Use &amp; Recovery</h2>
          <p>
            Confidential treatment and recovery support for alcohol and substance use — free,
            judgment-free, and available around the clock.
          </p>
          <div class="redbar"></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="res-grid" id="recovery-grid"></div>
    </div>
    <div id="section-servicedogs" class="cat-section">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <div class="sec-head-icon">🦮</div>
        <div class="sec-head-text">
          <h2>Service Dogs</h2>
          <p>
            Organizations that train and place service dogs at no cost for veterans living with
            PTSD, traumatic brain injury, or mobility needs, serving Alabama and the Southeast.
          </p>
          <div class="redbar"></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="res-grid" id="servicedogs-grid"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="res-suggest">
      <h3>Don’t See What You Need?</h3>
      <p>
        We are always adding resources. Tell us what is missing, or print this guide to share with a
        veteran who needs it.
      </p>
      <div class="rs-btns">
        <button
          class="rs-btn"
          onclick="
              openContact();
              return false;
            "
        >
          Suggest a Resource</button
        ><button class="rs-btn-o" onclick="window.print()">Print This Guide</button>
      </div>
      <div
        style="
            margin-top: 24px;
            font-size: 11px;
            letter-spacing: 1px;
            text-transform: uppercase;
            color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.42);
          "
      >
        Directory last reviewed August 1, 2026 · Next review by September 30, 2026
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
